From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/38] fs: sharedfs: keep unlinked files usable while open

POSIX keeps a file usable after unlink for as long as it is open or
mapped. The host frees the index slot at unlink, so a request for a new
chunk of such a file found no entry and failed with ESTALE.

The driver now tracks readers as well as writers per inode number and
tells the daemon about the first and last of each; the daemon keeps a
read handle and a write handle, keyed by inode number, and resolves
requests through them when the entry is gone. Attribute changes to an
unlinked open file are applied to the inode directly, as there is no
index entry to refresh it from. After a resume from hibernation every
open file is reopened on the new daemon.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
